          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "the genet (also jenet), a kind of civet-cat native to southern Europe, west Asia and Africa; (pl.) the skins of the animal employed as fur for garments (Veale 219). Black skins were more valuable than grey; the best were taken in season, i.e. killed in winter when the animal is normally hunted (Veale 25)."
    }
  ],
